## 4. First-Level Diagnostic Checklist

Before editing files:

- [ ] Read the full error message.
- [ ] Identify the command or user action that triggered it.
- [ ] Record the relevant endpoint or component.
- [ ] Check whether the issue happens consistently.
- [ ] Inspect recent changes using Git.
- [ ] Verify environment variables are present.
- [ ] Check whether required services are running.
- [ ] Reproduce the issue with the smallest possible input.
- [ ] Check whether a related test already exists.

### Check Git Changes

Run these commands from the repository root:

```bash
git status
git diff
git diff --stat
```

Review the output before changing or reverting anything. Do not discard uncommitted work without explicit approval.

