## 13. Deployment Debugging

When the project works locally but fails after deployment, compare local and production conditions.

### Deployment Checklist

- [ ] Correct frontend root directory.
- [ ] Correct backend root directory.
- [ ] Correct build command.
- [ ] Correct start command.
- [ ] Required environment variables configured.
- [ ] Correct production API URL.
- [ ] Database reachable from the hosting environment.
- [ ] Required dependencies installed.
- [ ] Build completes successfully.
- [ ] Logs show a successful startup.
- [ ] CORS permits the intended frontend origin.
- [ ] Persistent storage requirements are satisfied.
- [ ] Health checks work where configured.

Do not assume that separate frontend and backend deployments are automatically misconfigured. Verify their URLs, networking, environment variables, and API contracts.

### Logs to Inspect

Use the logs provided by the relevant hosting platform.

Check:

- Build logs.
- Application startup logs.
- Runtime exceptions.
- Failed HTTP requests.
- Database connection errors.
- Missing environment variables.
- Health-check failures.

Redact sensitive values before sharing logs for debugging.

